---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/privacy.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Events Privacy Policy"
  description="Bay Area Tech and AI Events privacy policy. No personal data collected."
>
  <main id="main" class="privacy-page grid-page">
    <a href="/events/" class="back-link">&larr; Events</a>

    <header class="privacy-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: November 8, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What This Page Does</h2>
      <p>
        The Bay Area Tech and AI Events page displays the tech and AI events Luma is currently
        listing for the Bay Area. It runs in your browser, and it can optionally sync your choices
        between your devices (see Optional Sync below).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <p>
        This page does <strong>not</strong> use accounts or sign-in, and it does not ask for contact information.
        It does make the network requests needed to load event data and run website analytics:
      </p>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li>Event data is fetched from this website's public data files</li>
        <li>
          When you use Current intent, your browser downloads a matching model from Hugging Face
        </li>
        <li>No cookies set by this page</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This website uses Google Analytics to understand which pages are visited and how long
        visitors stay. Google's <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="privacy-link">privacy policy</a
        > applies to that data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Event Data</h2>
      <p>
        Event listings are fetched from a public source and displayed directly in your browser. No
        personal data is included in these requests.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Current Intent</h2>
      <p>
        Your Current intent text is matched in your browser. It is not saved to local storage, sent
        to this site, or included in optional sync. Your browser downloads the matching model only
        when you use this feature; that request does not include your text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Local Storage</h2>
      <p>
        Your selected locations, selected days, New filter, excluded keywords, and applied or
        ignored events are saved using the browser's local storage. Applied and ignored events are
        deleted after 7 days. This data stays on your device unless you clear it in your browser.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Optional Sync</h2>
      <p>
        Your filter and handled-event choices leave your browser only if you choose to sync. If you
        create a sync code, this page sends your selected locations, selected days, New filter,
        excluded keywords, and applied or ignored events (with the event name, date, location, and
        host fields) to this site's sync storage, so your other devices can read the same settings.
        Your sync code is stored only as a one-way hash, so the site cannot read it back. Anyone who
        has the code can read and change those settings. Disconnecting a device removes the code
        from that device only. Synced settings are kept until you rotate or stop using the code.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted here.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Reach out at <a href="/events/" class="privacy-link">kunli.co/events</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
